# Project Overview

## Stack
- Python

## Directory Structure
```
worker-project/                 # Project and git repo root
├── worker/                     # Package name
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── __main__.py             # Enables: python -m worker if needed (i.e. if only a default cli no arg invocation possible)
│   ├── cli/
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   └── commands.py         # CLI commands to run task/tasks the worker can perform
│   ├── tasks/                  # Tasks the worker can perform (can be one to many)
│   │   └── __init__.py
│   ├── config.py               # Configuration settings for the workers task
│   ├── models/                 # Can be database models if needed or Pydantic models for validation and schema definition
│   │   └── __init__.py
│   └── utils/                  # Utility functions for the worker task
│       └── __init__.py
├── tests/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── conftest.py
├── pyproject.toml
├── uv.lock
├── README.md
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
└── LICENSE
```

## Key Principles
- Security-first approach
- Clean code practices

## Git Commits
- Use conventional commit prefixes (feat:, fix:, etc.)
- Keep messages concise and reference issues

## Security
- No secrets in code
- Validate inputs
- Encrypt sensitive data
